  "Blueprint (91be37cd) documentUpdate: inserted '## Documents (read in this order)' before the final artifact-link line: Blueprint, Contracts, project Contract section, Roster + 9 character sheets, Threat Model, Execution Schedule, Golden Path, then 'Waiting on the issue cap' with all 11 live pending-issue documents (the critique said 12; only 11 exist) and the FIX-5 folded-spec note. No other Blueprint text changed.",
  "Read-first paragraph appended to the Goal section of PAP-92, PAP-13, PAP-91, PAP-103, PAP-114, PAP-219, PAP-279, PAP-96, PAP-25 (marker '**Read first.**'), each with an issue-specific pointer (e.g. Contracts \u00a75 for PAP-13, Threat Model \u00a74-6 for PAP-96, NJ-2 for PAP-25).",
  "'Contract source:' bullet appended to the Interface contract of 29 issues citing Contracts sections by number and \u00a76 matrix row: Principal PAP-55/35/267/59; Money PAP-71/164/175/180/187; FilterTree PAP-279/161/116/119; event envelope PAP-28/97/136/174/177; gate artifacts PAP-78/80/82/83/84/85/89/239; Threat Model PAP-219/80/81/106 (and PAP-177 \u00a78 PCI). PAP-219 and PAP-279 got both a read-first and a contract-source.",
  "PAP-92: 'Required reading order' Spec bullet rewritten to list the documents first; DoD gained the line 'links every document ... and states the umbrella, promotion and deferred rules'. FIX-8 agent: PAP-92 now names the promotion rule (PAP-96 promotion package, PAP-93 BLOCKED_BY_OPEN, branch-start rule) in its DoD; put the rule text itself under a Spec heading 'How your issue got to Ready'.",
  "All edits are read-modify-write on live descriptions fetched in the same batch (10 issues per request, 4 requests + 1 read + 1 documentUpdate + verification); idempotent via markers, safe to re-run. No issues created, no relations, no states, no labels, no views, no PAP-1..12 touched.",
  "Verification 06:44Z: 36/36 target issues link interface-and-data-contracts; Blueprint has 11 pending-doc links and 9 character-sheet links; PAP-92 links Blueprint, Contracts, Threat Model, Roster, Schedule, Golden Path."
